Package: hydrofabric
Title: Build Hydrologic Modeling Fabrics from Reference Networks
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Mike",
           family = "Johnson",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "mjohnson@lynker.com"),
    person(given = "Lynker Corporation",
           role = "cph"),
    person(given = "NOAA Office of Water Prediction",
           role = "fnd",
           comment = "partial funding"))
Description: A general toolkit for building hydrologic modeling fabrics from a
    reference hydrographic network. Flowlines are split, collapsed, and
    reconciled against flow direction and flow accumulation rasters; catchment
    divides are partitioned to match; the network is aggregated to a
    distribution topology; and per-unit results are merged into global domains
    with globally unique identifiers. Outputs are checked against structural invariants
    and stamped with build provenance for reproducible reuse. The reference
    application is the NOAA Office of Water Prediction National Water Model
    (NWM) v4 for the NextGen Modeling System, developed with partial OWP
    funding.
